{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Fix Linter & Pre-commit Issues",
  "description": "Automatically runs linting tools (ruff, mypy) and pre-commit hooks to fix code quality issues and ensure all problems are resolved before committing",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "*.py",
      "pyproject.toml",
      ".pre-commit-config.yaml",
      "requirements.txt"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Run the following commands to fix all linting and pre-commit issues:\n\n1. Fix code formatting and style issues:\n   - Run `ruff check --fix .` to auto-fix style violations\n   - Run `ruff format .` to apply consistent formatting\n   - Run `mypy src/` to check type annotations\n\n2. Run pre-commit hooks to catch any remaining issues:\n   - Run `pre-commit run --all-files` to execute all configured hooks\n   - If any hooks fail, fix the reported issues and re-run\n\n3. Verify all issues are resolved:\n   - Run `ruff check .` to ensure no remaining style violations\n   - Run `mypy src/` to confirm type checking passes\n   - Run `pre-commit run --all-files` again to verify all hooks pass\n\n4. Check specific PlantGuard requirements:\n   - Ensure all functions have complete type annotations\n   - Verify no bare `except:` clauses exist\n   - Confirm `logger.info()` is used instead of `print()` in production code\n   - Check that `pathlib.Path` is used for file operations\n   - Validate line length is ≤100 characters\n\nFix any remaining issues found and ensure the codebase is ready for commit."
  }
}
